==============================================================================
SPECIAL PERMISSIONS AUDIT
==============================================================================

This report documents special permission files that should be reviewed for
security compliance. SUID/SGID/Sticky bit permissions can pose security risks
if not properly managed.

Note: A comprehensive audit should be performed manually using:
- SUID files: find / -xdev -type f -perm -4000 2>/dev/null
- SGID files: find / -xdev -type f -perm -2000 2>/dev/null
- Sticky bit: find / -xdev -type d -perm -1000 2>/dev/null

Common SUID/SGID binaries that are typically expected:
- /usr/bin/sudo (SUID)
- /usr/bin/su (SUID)
- /bin/passwd (SUID)
- /usr/bin/chsh (SUID)
- /usr/bin/chfn (SUID)
- /usr/libexec/pt_chown (SUID)

Review any other SUID/SGID files for necessity and consider removal if
not required for system operation.
